# SYNOPSIS

```usage
true
```

# DESCRIPTION

`true` does nothing and exits 0.
It ignores any arguments.

`true` is sbase's, built into `sbase-box` with sbase's other commands and installed as `/boot/bin/posix/true`, a hard link to it.
In the POSIX namespace (a manifest's `ns=posix`, made by `/lib/ns/posix`, see namespace(6)) `/boot/bin/posix` is bound before `/boot/bin` on `/bin`, so POSIX programs find it as `/bin/true`.
There is no native `true`.

# SEE ALSO

false(1), test(1); sbase's page is `third_party/sbase/true.1` in the repository

# DIAGNOSTICS

None: the exit status is always 0.
